    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> alexcrichton submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15051#pullrequestreview-5690727215\">PR review</a>.</p>",
        "id": 636056339,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793291074
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15051#discussion_r4413783261\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Might be worth pointing out that <code>false</code> is a lie here, but it kind of doesn't matter. Or perhaps alternatively, could there be a separate <code>struct_get_{s,u}</code> helper and then there's no param here at all? It's a bit odd to have that flag as well for floats for example.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 636056345,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793291075
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15051#discussion_r4413824955\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Technically speaking one theoretical optimization here could be if in the GC ABI the src/destination are immutable and equal the exact struct could be plumbed through as-is, right? (fine to leave for a future PR/issue, just want to confirm my understanding)</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 636056346,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793291075
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15051#discussion_r4406926706\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>In theory these are pretty easy, right? Mostly just <code>abstract_(...)</code>?</p>\n<p>IIRC <code>ConcreteExn</code> won't show up here, although I'm not sure about continuations.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 636056347,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793291075
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15051#discussion_r4406915006\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Instead of <code>.unwrap()</code> could this be <code>let Ok(()) = ...</code>?</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 636056348,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793291075
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15051#discussion_r4406948401\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>There's no max for the GC ABI, right?</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 636056349,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793291075
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15051#discussion_r4413803812\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Instead of duplicating this comment in all blocks, could there be an explanatory comment in one location and the others briefly redirect to that?</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 636056350,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793291075
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15051#discussion_r4406913051\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This is a linear search in a loop which might lead to quadratic behavior I think -- could <code>idx</code> here, since it's a module-local thing, be compare to the first index in the rec group instead?</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 636056356,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793291076
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15051#discussion_r4413965466\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Not that it matters for this test, but technically the <code>(rec ...)</code> here isn't necessary right?</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 636056357,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793291076
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15051#discussion_r4413744525\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>FWIW I think that the concurrent code is going to need some relatively invasive changes to handle the GC ABI. Not only because of rooting everywhere but also because limits/maximums in params/results are pretty heavily baked in to the implementation on the host side. It might be best to just reject this for now and have a separate <code>todo!</code> or component-model-async integration being a big TODO item.</p>\n<p>For example there's <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/blob/bcc6af9cfd38b1b9b3c190cda5704d2d5fb036c0/crates/wasmtime/src/runtime/component/concurrent.rs#L3053\">code like this</a> which is definitely not correct for GC.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 636056358,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793291076
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15051#discussion_r4413705873\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I'm a bit confused by this, aren't all interface types representable with a single core wasm type in the GC ABI meaning that <code>flat_val_types</code> should always succeed for GC?</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 636056359,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793291076
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15051#discussion_r4413904898\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This feels relatively confusing to me because GC tuples do indeed have a single flat type, so this method is kind of a lie in that respect. Could this method grow documentation about how it's supposed to be used or perhaps renamed to cater to the use case for how this works at call-sites?</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 636056361,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793291076
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15051#discussion_r4413815016\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>How come these extra vecs are made?</p>\n</blockquote>",
