    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> fitzgen created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15051#discussion_r4417440249\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Not really because <code>Destination::Stack</code> holds <code>&amp;[ValType]</code> which doesn't work for <code>i8</code>/<code>i16</code>, but even if we turned it into <code>&amp;[StorageType]</code> then we would also need to know the which field of the struct it is and at this point the sharing is not really that helpful. I think <code>Destination::Struct</code> starts making more sense as we start supporting nested tuples in <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15054\">https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15054</a>, e.g.:</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/fitzgen/wasmtime/blob/1706336c1f96c0ff5ffcb6a347511b3c339acb55/crates/environ/src/fact/trampoline.rs#L1242-L1248\">https://github.com/fitzgen/wasmtime/blob/1706336c1f96c0ff5ffcb6a347511b3c339acb55/crates/environ/src/fact/trampoline.rs#L1242-L1248</a></p>\n</blockquote>",
