    {
        "content": "<p>fitzgen <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15051#issuecomment-6507441264\">commented</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15051\">PR #15051</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>@alexcrichton I believe I have addressed all of your review feedback with the latest commit </p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 636114909,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793305304
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> alexcrichton submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15051#pullrequestreview-5705558368\">PR review</a>.</p>",
        "id": 636135457,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793311676
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15051#discussion_r4418388441\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Could this return not a <code>GcStruct</code> but perhaps the internals of the type, such as a local/type? It feels a bit odd to need sentinel values for <code>field</code> and e.g. <code>FIELD_UNSET</code> in the next PR where I think it would be best to model this as the <code>GcStruct</code> destination is directly created in <code>aggregate_field_srcs</code>' iterator.</p>\n<p>Also, to confirm, I'd expect in the next PR that this method would take <code>&amp;mut Compiler</code> to fill out the struct <code>todo!</code> here by injecting a <code>struct.get</code> instruction to get a struct-from-a-struct</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 636135458,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793311677
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15051#discussion_r4418410012\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I'm not totally sold on this myself just yet, it seems like this would ideally use <code>Destination::Stack</code> for GC types and <code>translate_{tuple,record}</code> would have custom follow-ups for the GC ABI which inserts a <code>struct.new</code> with the desired type. The <code>Destination::Stack</code> variant has all the types expected as well as <code>Options</code> which seems like a good fit for all of this.</p>\n<p>Furthermore the handling of <code>Destination::Struct</code> already does nothing everywhere which is basically the same for <code>stack_set</code> when the types line up (which they always would for the GC ABI).</p>\n<p>Did you have other plans in mind for <code>Destination::Struct</code> in the future though? </p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 636135459,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793311677
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15051#discussion_r4418371772\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Question on this: why is this needed? I would naively expect that all GC structs are required to store a component-model <code>u8</code> in a storage-type <code>i8</code> field, so wouldn't this be dead code in such a situation? Or is this one where a storage of <code>i32</code> matches a component model <code>u8</code> type?</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 636135461,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793311677
    }
]